losing_improve_gpt5nano:
Great question. To assess PhD programs in Business, ask for concrete career outcomes and clear details about support. Here's a tighter version you can post:

I'm evaluating PhD programs in Business and want specific information on career outcomes and networking support. For current/former students and alumni, please share:
- your program's job-placement rate within 2–3 years after graduation, broken down by sector (academia, industry/consulting/analytics, government, etc.) and location;
- the career services available to PhD students (career advisor, CV/resume reviews, mock interviews, workshops, networking events);
- the strength of the alumni network and how you access mentoring, introductions to employers, internships, or project opportunities;
- typical paths graduates take (academic vs non-academic) and whether MBA holders enter the PhD with similar timelines or different tracks;
- any industry partnerships, research centers, or sponsored projects that help with placements;
- funding/assistantship details and expectations for PhD students.

If you have links or contacts to share, please include them. Thanks!

